# Supabase Clients

| Client | Import | Use when |
|--------|--------|---------|
| Server (session-aware) | `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` | Server components, API routes, middleware |
| Admin (bypasses RLS) | `createAdminClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/admin` | Privileged ops only (webhooks, invitations) |
| Browser | `createBrowserClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client` | Client components needing direct Supabase access |

# Query Functions

All data access goes through `src/lib/supabase/queries.ts` — never inline Supabase queries in page or API route files.

`getCurrentUserProfile(userId)` is wrapped in React `cache()` — safe and efficient to call multiple times per request.

# Type Mapping Convention

DB rows use `snake_case`; application types use `camelCase`. Each entity has:
- `*Row` interface — raw DB shape (snake_case)
- Domain type in `src/types/` — camelCase, dates as `Date` objects

Mapping happens inside `queries.ts` via helper functions like `dbToMember()`, `dbToOrganization()`.

# Key Tables

| Table | Notes |
|-------|-------|
| `organizations` | Has `trial_ends_at`, `stripe_customer_id` |
| `profiles` | Users within an org; has `role` (`owner`/`staff`) |
| `members` | Clients of the wellness center |
| `visits` | Appointments/bookings |
| `event_types` | Services (e.g. massage, yoga class) |
| `event_categories` | Groups for event types |
| `subscriptions` | One row per Stripe subscription lifecycle event; current state = latest row for org |
| `invitations` | Staff invite tokens |

# Migrations

Migrations live in `supabase/migrations/` with numeric prefix: `038_add_trial_to_organizations.sql`.
Seed data is in `supabase/seed.sql`.
